-- title:
--   Verschiebung isomorphisms on the torus quotient of the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a modulus $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ such that every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial already lies in $H$ (hypotheses `hpM`, `hpM2`, `hHp`). Fix further a valuation subring $Pl$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $Pl$ (`hPl`) and with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, and the hypothesis `hj` that the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqModC ℚ`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) lies in the subfield [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) generated by the integral form ratios at level $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$; $\mathfrak{X}$ is a model datum [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`](def/ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP.html#L81) over the localisation `R p` of $\mathbb{Q}$ at $p$, $\Lambda$ is level data and $O$ is a Néron object [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM Pl hPl Λ`](def/ModularCurve_JHNeronObjectAtP.html#L53), so that in particular $O$ provides a smooth separated group scheme $O.G \to$ base over `R p` with relative group law `O.L`, an identification of [`ModularCurve.JH M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L127) with the generic sections, and Hecke endomorphisms. The two hypotheses `hrep` and `hrepΛ` require that the sub-Picard condition `algEquivZeroCut` for the two-chart integral model at level $\Gamma_M$ (respectively at level $\Gamma_N$, with the rigidification $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ composed with $\mathfrak{X}.\pi$) be represented, in the sense of `RepresentsRelSubPic`, by the designation built from $O.G$, $O.g$ and the unit section of `O.L` (respectively from $\Lambda.X$, $\Lambda.f$ and the unit section of $\Lambda.L$).
--
--   The coefficient ring $Rh$ is a Henselian local domain which is an $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra with faithful scalar action, whose image lies in $Pl$ (`hRA`) and whose maximal ideal consists exactly of the elements of $Pl$-valuation $< 1$ (`hRloc`); it carries in addition a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra structure whose kernel is again cut out by the condition of valuation $< 1$ (`hres`).
--
--   Over $Rh$ there is given a $p$-divisible group $\mathcal{G}$ of height $h$, that is, a tower of finite free cocommutative Hopf $Rh$-algebras $\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,v$ of rank $p^{vh}$ with surjective transition maps whose kernels are the $p^v$-torsion ideals. It is compared with the Jacobian by an additive map $\Delta$ from the points of $\mathcal{G}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to [`ModularCurve.JH M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L127) and a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-linear map $e$ on Tate modules, subject to the following groups of hypotheses, whose content is summarised here: injectivity of $\Delta$ (`hΔinj`); the level identification `hΔlev`, that `O.finPts (p ^ v)` is exactly the image under $\Delta$ of the level-$v$ points; Galois equivariance of $\Delta$ for automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ which are $Rh$-linear (`hΔgal`); the Hecke compatibility `hΔhecke`, that each generator $g$ of [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) is realised by a transition-compatible family of Hopf endomorphisms $\varphi_v$ of the tower inducing [`ModularCurve.genOpH M H S g`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L80) through $\Delta$; the clauses `he`, `heinj`, `herange`, `hegal` and `hsat` describing $e$ as the coordinatewise map induced by $\Delta$, injective, with image the Tate vectors whose $n$-th entry lies in `O.finPts (p ^ n)`, Galois equivariant for [`ModularCurve.JH.tateGaloisRep`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L154), and saturated for multiplication by $p$; the hypothesis `hcoker` that the cokernel of $e$ is free of rank `O.toricRank` over $\mathbb{Z}_p$; and `htor`, that the $p^v$-toric points `O.toricPts (p ^ v)` lie in the image of the level-$v$ points under $\Delta$.
--
--   A second $p$-divisible group $\mathcal{B}$ over $Rh$, of height $hB$, is given together with a family of Hopf algebra maps $\psi_v : \mathcal{B}.\mathrm{level}\,v \to \mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,v$, the numerical hypotheses $h = O.\mathrm{toricRank} + hB$ and $hB = 2h'$ for some $h'$ (`hhB`, `hhB2`), and the clauses `hψt` (compatibility with the transitions), `hψker` (a level-$v$ point $x$ of $\mathcal{G}$ pulls back along $\psi_v$ to the identity point of $\mathcal{B}$ precisely when $\Delta$ of $x$ lies in `O.toricPts (p ^ v)`), `hψsurj` (every level-$v$ point of $\mathcal{B}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is such a pull-back), `hψred` (if the $\psi_v$-pull-back of $x$ agrees with the counit to $Pl$-valuation $< 1$ on all of $\mathcal{B}.\mathrm{level}\,v$, then $x$ does so on all of $\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,v$), and `hperiod` (for $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup `Pl.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, for $z$ in the $p^v$-torsion [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.torsion`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L244) of the Jacobian of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionFieldBar M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L123), and for a level-$v$ point $y$ with $\Delta(y) = \sigma \cdot z - z$, the $\psi_v$-pull-back of $y$ agrees with the counit to valuation $< 1$).
--
--   The scheme-theoretic interface consists of a ring map $\rho_h : \,$`R p`$\, \to Rh$ compatible with the algebra maps to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hρh`) and a family of morphisms $\iota_v : \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,v) \to O.G$ subject to: `hιbase` (each $\iota_v$ lies over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho_h$); `hιcl` (the induced morphism to the fibre product is a closed immersion); `hιp` ($\iota_v$ composed with multiplication by $p^v$ in `O.L` factors through the unit section); `hιpts` (the section of $O$ attached by `O.pts` to $\Delta$ of a level-$v$ point is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of that point followed by $\iota_v$); `hιmul` (compatibility of $\iota_v$ with the group law `O.L.mul` for points over any $Rh$-algebra $B$); `hιt` (compatibility with the transition maps); `hιhecke` (each Hecke generator is realised by a transition-compatible family of Hopf endomorphisms $\varphi_v$ which intertwines $\iota_v$ with `O.hecke S g` and induces [`ModularCurve.genOpH M H S g`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L80) through $\Delta$); and `hιfin`, which asserts that the morphism $j_v$ induced by $\iota_v$ into the base change along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho_h$ of the $p^v$-torsion of `O.L` is simultaneously an open and a closed immersion, and that every point of that base change lying over the closed point of $Rh$ belongs to the range of the underlying map of $j_v$.
--
--   Finally, `hjB` requires that $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes \psi_v$, in the form `Bialgebra.TensorProduct.map (BialgHom.id (ZMod p) (ZMod p)) (ψ v)`, be injective for every $v$, and a torus-quotient tower is given: types $T v$ which are commutative rings, cocommutative Hopf $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebras, finite and free over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, with transition maps $t^T_v : T(v+1) \to T v$ and bialgebra maps $\pi^T_v : \mathbb{Z}/p \otimes_{Rh} \mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,v \to T v$, satisfying: each $t^T_v$ is surjective (`htT`), $\operatorname{finrank}_{\mathbb{Z}/p} T v = p^{v \cdot O.\mathrm{toricRank}}$ (`hrankT`), $\ker t^T_v$ is the $p^v$-torsion ideal [`PDivisibleGroup.Hopf.torsionIdeal (ZMod p) (T (v+1)) (p ^ v)`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L157) (`hkerT`), each $\pi^T_v$ is surjective (`hπT`), the squares relating $\pi^T$ with the transitions of $\mathcal{G}$ and with $t^T$ commute (`hπTt`), and the exactness clause `hexT`: the kernel of $\pi^T_v$ is the ideal generated by the image under $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes \psi_v$ of the kernel of the counit of $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes_{Rh} \mathcal{B}.\mathrm{level}\,v$.
--
--   The conclusion is the existence of a family $\mathrm{Ver}^T$ assigning to every $v \in \mathbb{N}$ a bialgebra isomorphism $\mathrm{Ver}^T_v : T v \to T v$ over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ such that for every $v$ and every $\chi$ in the Cartier dual [`CartierDual (ZMod p) (T v)`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12) one has $\mathrm{CartierDual.map}(\mathrm{Ver}^T_v)(\chi) = \chi^p$, the $p$-th power being taken in the Cartier dual. No compatibility of the family $\mathrm{Ver}^T$ with the transition maps $t^T_v$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the statement that the torus quotient of the special fibre of the finite part of the Néron object of $J_H(M)$ at $p$ is of multiplicative type, expressed through the standard criterion that the Verschiebung be an isomorphism with $p$-th power dual. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.exists_torusQuotient_multiplicative_exact_raynaudQuotient_finPts_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_finPtsWitness`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_torusQuotient_multiplicative_exact_raynaudQuotient_finPts_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_finPtsWitness), which combines multiplicativity with the exactness of the Raynaud quotient sequence in the analysis of the $p$-adic Tate module of $J_H(M)$ at the prime $p$ exactly dividing the level.
